---
// The chrome both /design/ao/ pages wear: the ground, the column, the h1 and the small
// print. Split out of the merged logo page rather than duplicated into each half, because
// `<style is:global>` in a page ships only on that page and these rules are the one thing
// the write-up and the bench genuinely share.
//
// Not in global.css: that stylesheet ships on every route, including the blog and the home
// page, and none of this belongs there.
---
<style is:global>
  .lab { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 84px 24px 96px; }
  /* The page title sits above the demo rather than inside .lab, so that the document's
     first heading is this h1 and not the demo's "Download" h2. Styled by its own class,
     never by a descendant selector: the in-situ panel renders the real hero, whose own
     h1 must keep the bare `h1` rule in global.css. A `.lab h1` here outranked it and
     shrank the wordmark to 24px. The stroke and shadow resets are that same global rule
     in the other direction -- at 1400px it puts a 2.8px stroke on 24px text. */
  .la-title {
    max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 84px 24px 0;
    font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    -webkit-text-stroke: 0; text-shadow: none;
  }
  .lab > section > h2, .lab > h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 56px 0 8px; }
  .lab-hint { color: rgba(var(--color-primary-rgb), 0.55); font-size: 0.82rem; margin: 6px 0 0; }
</style>
